**Suggestion:** The `toggleChallenge` function does not handle the case where the `selected` array exceeds the `maxChallenges` limit. While the UI disables further selection, this logic should also be enforced at the function level to prevent unexpected behavior if the function is called programmatically.  
<details>
<summary><b>Severity Level:</b> Minor ⚠️</summary>

- ⚠️ Without this check, programmatic calls to `toggleChallenge` could bypass the UI restriction, leading to inconsistent state.
- ⚠️ This could result in more than the allowed number of challenges being selected.

</details>

```typescript
const toggleChallenge = (key: string) => {
  if (selected.includes(key)) {
    onChange(selected.filter(k => k !== key));
  } else if (selected.length < maxChallenges) {
    onChange([...selected, key]);
  } else {
    console.warn(`Cannot select more than ${maxChallenges} challenges.`);
  }
};
```

